COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.projection_scenarios IS 'The named scenarios (lever sets) of the Projection module; the one with is_default is the plan of record. Grain: one row per scenario. Source: public.proj_scenarios without the params blob (read the levers through projection_levers). Refresh: on edit. Coverage: about 7 scenarios. Caveats: archived_at set = deleted (kept 30 days): filter archived_at IS NULL for live scenarios. The model''s OUTPUT (P&L, cash, financing results) is computed by the app on demand and is not stored; read it from the HTTP API /api/projection/..., and read the inputs here.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.scenario_id IS 'Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.slug IS 'Unique slug.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.name IS 'Name.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.base_slug IS 'Fallback scenario for series cells this one does not hold.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.is_default IS 'true for the plan of record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.version IS '+1 on every change.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.frozen IS 'true = a frozen clone that no longer reads its base.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.created_at IS 'Created.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.updated_at IS 'Updated.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_scenarios.archived_at IS 'Set when the scenario was deleted (kept 30 days); NULL = live.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.projection_levers IS 'Every lever of every live scenario, one row per (scenario, module, lever): financing terms, driver rates (sales tax, channel shares), cohort levers (curve source, cohorts averaged), pacing and inventory settings. Grain: one row per (scenario_slug, module, lever). Source: public.proj_scenarios.params, flattened two levels deep. Refresh: on edit. Coverage: every live scenario. Caveats: value is json: a number, text, a list or a nested object depending on the lever. Cast with value #>> ''{}'' for scalars. | A scenario holds only the levers it changes; the app falls back to base_slug and then to code defaults, which are not rows here.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_levers.scenario_slug IS 'proj_scenarios.slug.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_levers.module IS 'Projection module that owns the lever: financing | drivers | cohorts | pacing | inventory_demand | inventory_supply | pnl ...';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_levers.lever IS 'Lever name inside the module (for example sales_tax_rate in drivers, curve_source in cohorts).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.projection_levers.value IS 'The lever''s value as json.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.projection_series IS 'The monthly cells a scenario itself holds: inputs (''input'') and overrides (''override'') of a line for a month. Grain: one row per (scenario_slug, line_key, month). Source: public.proj_series joined to public.proj_scenarios. Refresh: on edit. Coverage: about 1.6K cells. Caveats: Only cells the scenario itself holds; cells it inherits from its base scenario are not repeated here.';
