COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.cohorts_monthly IS 'One row per acquisition month: new customers, first-order dollars per customer and in total, CAC, 90-day repeat rate and payback as exported. Grain: one row per cohort_month. Source: public.proj_cohorts (cohort export uploads). Refresh: monthly upload. Coverage: about 33 cohorts. Caveats: Only closed months belong in the model (a month that is not over is blanked on upload). Cohort dollars differ by export source (Shopify vs Upstack): do not mix sources between refreshes. | cac and repeat_90d for the newest cohorts can be blank until final.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.cohort_month IS 'First of the acquisition month.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.new_customers IS 'Customers acquired.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.first_order_per_customer IS 'Average first-order $ per customer.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.first_order_revenue IS 'new_customers x first_order_per_customer: the cohort''s first-order revenue (the base the repeat curve multiplies).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.first_order_realized IS 'Same after refunds, reference only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.repeat_90d IS '90-day repeat rate (fraction).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.cac IS 'Cost to acquire a customer as exported.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.payback_months IS 'Payback period in months.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.nc_rev_reference IS 'New-customer revenue typed on the sheet, used only to tie the engine out.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.source IS 'Source label.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_monthly.loaded_at IS 'When loaded.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative IS 'Cumulative dollars per cohort customer at each age (months after acquisition), with the monthly increment, the increment as a multiple of the first order and the cohort''s recency rank at that age: the exact inputs of the Live retention curve. Grain: one row per (cohort_month, age). Source: public.proj_cohort_cum joined to public.proj_cohorts and itself (age - 1). Refresh: monthly upload. Coverage: about 33 cohorts x 36 ages. Caveats: Mirrors app/projection/cohorts/engine.py: a cell counts only when cum_per_customer is non-null and non-zero; the increment at age 1 is measured from first_order_per_customer. | Live curve at age a = sum(new_customers x increment_ratio) / sum(new_customers) over the rows with usable_rank <= N (N = the cohorts_n lever, 3 in code, 6 on the sheet); ages from tail_from_age (28) on = previous age x tail_decay (0.95). usable_rank 1 = the newest cohort that has a usable increment at that age.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative.cohort_month IS 'proj_cohorts.cohort_month.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative.age IS 'Months after acquisition (1-36).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative.new_customers IS 'Customers in the cohort (the weight in the Live curve).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative.first_order_per_customer IS 'The cohort''s first-order dollars per customer.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative.cum_per_customer IS 'Cumulative $ per customer, first order included.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative.increment IS 'Dollars per customer earned in this month of age: cum_per_customer minus the previous age (age 1: minus the first order). NULL when this or the previous cell is not observed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative.increment_ratio IS 'increment / first_order_per_customer: repeat dollars per $1 of first-order dollars in this month of age (the curve''s unit).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_cumulative.usable_rank IS '1 = the newest cohort whose increment_ratio at this age is usable (non-null, non-zero, new_customers > 0), 2 = the next, ...; NULL when this cell is not usable.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.cohorts_curve_goal IS 'Goal retention curve snapshots: repeat dollars per $1 of first-order revenue by age 1..60. The newest snapshot (is_active) is the Goal curve the model uses. Grain: one row per (snapshot_id, age). Source: public.proj_curve_goal without saved_by. Refresh: on save. Coverage: 60 rows per saved snapshot.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_goal.snapshot_id IS 'Snapshot id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_goal.snapshot_date IS 'Snapshot date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_goal.age IS 'Age in months (1-60).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_goal.value IS 'Repeat $ per $1 of first-order revenue.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_goal.note IS 'Note.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_goal.saved_at IS 'When saved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_goal.restored_from IS 'snapshot_id this is a copy of.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.cohorts_curve_goal.is_active IS 'true on every row of the newest snapshot (the highest snapshot_id), the one the model reads as the Goal curve.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.creative_family_daily IS 'Spend, purchases and revenue per creative family (tracker family) per day and stage, in three bases and for all ads or only the ads that were active that day. Grain: one row per (basis, ads_scope, family_key, day, stage). Source: public.family_daily, family_daily_active and their _upstack_nc / _upstack_all twins (rebuilt in full by etl.build_metrics), plus the product of the family''s first tracker row. Refresh: nightly (etl service 13:00 UTC). Coverage: 2026-05-06 through yesterday (Pacific); older days exist only in the sheet-era backfill. Caveats: basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases. | ads_scope: ''all_ads'' = every ad of the family; ''active_ads'' = only ads active that day. A family can span several tracker rows: key on family_key. | Filter basis and ads_scope in the WHERE clause: the planner then reads one table instead of six.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.basis IS 'basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.ads_scope IS '''all_ads'' | ''active_ads''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.family_key IS 'Tracker family key (lower).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.product_slug IS 'Product of the family''s first tracker row (NULL when the family has none).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.day IS 'Day (Meta ad account day).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.stage IS '''testing'' | ''scaling'' | ''unclassified'' (days with no campaign).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.spend IS 'Meta spend, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.purchases IS 'Meta-reported purchases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.revenue IS 'Meta-reported purchase value, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.link_clicks IS 'Link clicks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_daily.impressions IS 'Impressions over rows that carry them.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.creative_family_metrics IS 'Since-launch, 7-day and 30-day spend, purchases and revenue per tracker row, with impressions, clicks and the number of active ads, in three bases. Grain: one row per (basis, tracker_row_id). Source: public.ad_metrics and its _upstack_nc / _upstack_all twins (etl.build_metrics), with the tracker row''s concept id and the product. Refresh: nightly (etl service 13:00 UTC). Coverage: every live tracker row; spend from 2026-05-06. Caveats: basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases. | Metrics sit on the FIRST row of each ad family (is_first_row): sum rows, count unique ads with count(*) FILTER (WHERE is_first_row). | ''Launched'' (the denominator of the display hit rate) = first rows with a launch_date or any spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.basis IS 'basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.tracker_row_id IS 'tracker_rows.id (primary key).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.concept_id IS 'Creative Tracker concept id of the row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.family_key IS 'Tracker family key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.product_slug IS 'Product of the tracker row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.is_first_row IS 'true on the row that carries the family''s metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.launch_date IS 'Launch date of the row (tracker).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.spend_launch IS 'Since-launch spend, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.purchases_launch IS 'Since-launch Meta-reported purchases (rounded to whole numbers).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.revenue_launch IS 'Since-launch Meta-reported purchase value, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.spend_7d IS 'Spend over the 7 days ending the last complete day.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.purchases_7d IS 'Purchases over those 7 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.revenue_7d IS 'Purchase value over those 7 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.spend_30d IS 'Spend over the 30 days ending the last complete day.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.purchases_30d IS 'Purchases over those 30 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.revenue_30d IS 'Purchase value over those 30 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.live IS 'true when the family spent on either of the last two days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.impressions_launch IS 'Since-launch impressions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.clicks_launch IS 'Since-launch link clicks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.ads_active_count IS 'ACTIVE Meta ads of the family (same on every row of the family).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.spend_launch_active IS 'Since-launch spend of the ACTIVE ads only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.purchases_launch_active IS 'Since-launch purchases of the ACTIVE ads only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.revenue_launch_active IS 'Since-launch purchase value of the ACTIVE ads only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.impressions_launch_active IS 'Since-launch impressions of the ACTIVE ads only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.clicks_launch_active IS 'Since-launch link clicks of the ACTIVE ads only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.live_active IS 'true when the ACTIVE ads of the family spent on either of the last two days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_family_metrics.built_at IS 'When the table was built.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.creative_unmatched_meta IS 'Meta ad families that run on no Creative Tracker row, with their spend and results, in three bases. Grain: one row per (basis, family_key). Source: public.unmatched_meta and its twins (etl.build_metrics), with the product slug. Refresh: nightly (etl service 13:00 UTC). Coverage: families with Meta delivery since 2026-05-06. Caveats: basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.basis IS 'basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.family_key IS 'lower(Meta ad family) (primary key).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.family_name IS 'Display name (the variant with the highest lifetime spend).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.product_slug IS 'Product guessed from the family''s name, campaign or ad set (product_source says which).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.spend_7d IS 'Spend over the last 7 days, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.purchases_7d IS 'Purchases over the last 7 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.revenue_7d IS 'Purchase value over the last 7 days, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.spend_30d IS 'Spend over the last 30 days, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.purchases_30d IS 'Purchases over the last 30 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.revenue_30d IS 'Purchase value over the last 30 days, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.spend_all IS 'Spend over every day held in ad_daily, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.purchases_all IS 'Purchases over every day held.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.revenue_all IS 'Purchase value over every day held, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.live IS 'true when the family spent on either of the last two days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.spend_launch IS 'All-time lifetime spend (Meta API), dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.purchases_launch IS 'All-time lifetime purchases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.revenue_launch IS 'All-time lifetime purchase value, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.impressions_launch IS 'All-time impressions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.clicks_launch IS 'All-time link clicks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_unmatched_meta.product_source IS 'name | campaign | adset | none.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.creative_stage_moves IS 'Test to scale: one row per creative family with its testing and scaling spend and results, when it first spent in a Testing and in a Scaling campaign and whether it moved, in three bases. Grain: one row per (basis, family_key). Source: public.creative_stage_moves and its twins (etl.stage_moves, rebuilt nightly). Refresh: nightly (etl service 13:00 UTC). Coverage: 2026-05-06 through yesterday (Pacific). Caveats: basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases. | A creative MOVED when it spent in a Testing campaign and its first spend in a Scaling campaign came on a later day (campaign name contains ''test'' = Testing). Rate of reaching scaling = moved / began_in_testing over creatives launched in the window and not launched_before_data_start (app/promotions.py). | moves_that_day >= 40 (bulk_move_day) is a mass relaunch into new scaling campaigns, not a set of test winners: exclude it when judging test winners. | Held up? = (scale_revenue / scale_spend) / (test_revenue / test_spend): held >= 0.90, softer >= 0.70, fell below; too early until scale_spend >= $200 and scale_days >= 3.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.basis IS 'basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.family_key IS 'Tracker family key (lower); joins family_daily, ad_metrics, creative_assets.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.tracker_row_id IS 'tracker_rows.id of the family''s first row (the one that carries its metrics); the app opens /ad/<id>.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.product_slug IS 'Product slug (''unassigned'' for creatives of no product).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.product_name IS 'Product name.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.concept_id IS 'Concept id of the first tracker row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.display IS 'Display name: the ad family as typed in the tracker, else the concept id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.ad_type IS 'VID / IMG (tracker).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.tracker_status IS 'Tracker status of the first row, e.g. ''8 - Launched''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.tracker_launch_date IS 'Launch date typed in the tracker (undercounts the older ads; first_day is the one the page uses).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.cluster IS 'Market cluster of the current tag (''(untagged)'' when none).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.icp IS 'ICP of the current tag.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.pain_point IS 'Pain point of the current tag.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.data_start IS 'First day this view''s family_daily holds (2026-05-06 today).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.data_through IS 'Last day this view''s family_daily holds.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.path IS 'moved | testing_only | scaling_only | same_day (testing and scaling both first spent that day) | scaling_first (scaling before testing) | unclassified_only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.began_in_testing IS 'true for moved and testing_only: the creatives a test-to-scale rate is about.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.moved IS 'true when path = ''moved'': spent in testing and its first scaling day is later.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.first_day IS 'First day with spend in any stage = the launch day as far as the data goes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.testing_first_day IS 'First day with spend in a Testing campaign (NULL if none).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.scaling_first_day IS 'First day with spend in a Scaling campaign (NULL if none): the day of the move for a moved creative.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.last_spend_day IS 'Last day with spend in any stage.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.scaling_last_day IS 'Last day with spend in a Scaling campaign.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.days_in_test IS 'scaling_first_day - testing_first_day, for moved creatives only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.launched_before_data_start IS 'true when first_day is the first day of data: the creative was already running and its real launch day is earlier.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.test_spend IS 'Testing-stage spend on days before the first scaling day, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.test_purchases IS 'Purchases (Meta-reported here, Upstack in the _upstack_ views) on those days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.test_revenue IS 'Purchase value on those days, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.test_link_clicks IS 'Link clicks on those days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.test_days IS 'Days with testing spend before the first scaling day.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.test_after_spend IS 'Testing-stage spend on or after the first scaling day (the original kept running), dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.scale_spend IS 'Scaling-stage spend since the move, through the last day, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.scale_purchases IS 'Purchases in the Scaling stage.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.scale_revenue IS 'Purchase value in the Scaling stage, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.scale_link_clicks IS 'Link clicks in the Scaling stage.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.scale_days IS 'Days with scaling spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.unclassified_spend IS 'Spend on days with no campaign (stage ''unclassified''), dollars; none today.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.last7_spend IS 'Spend over the last 7 days of data, any stage, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.last7_purchases IS 'Purchases over the last 7 days, any stage.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.last7_revenue IS 'Purchase value over the last 7 days, any stage, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.last7_scale_spend IS 'Scaling-stage spend over the last 7 days, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.last7_scale_purchases IS 'Scaling-stage purchases over the last 7 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.last7_scale_revenue IS 'Scaling-stage purchase value over the last 7 days, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.live IS 'true when the creative spent on the last day of data or the day before (any stage).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.live_scaling IS 'true when it spent in a Scaling campaign on the last day of data or the day before.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.moves_that_day IS 'Creatives that moved on the same scaling_first_day (all creatives, not only this product).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_stage_moves.bulk_move_day IS 'true when moved and 40 or more creatives moved that day: a mass relaunch, not a test winner.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.creative_scaling_placements IS 'Where a creative that moved to scaling scales: its scaling campaign and ad set since the move, with spend and results, in three bases. Grain: one row per (basis, family_key, campaign_id, adset_id). Source: public.creative_scaling_placements and its twins (etl.stage_moves). Refresh: nightly (etl service 13:00 UTC). Coverage: creatives that moved since 2026-05-06. Caveats: basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.basis IS 'basis: ''meta'' (Meta-reported purchases and revenue, counts returning customers) | ''upstack_new_customers'' (Upstack first orders, any-click 30 days) | ''upstack_all_orders'' (every order Upstack credits). Spend and impressions are Meta''s in all three; filter basis = ''meta'' unless you mean an Upstack basis, and never add rows of different bases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.family_key IS 'Tracker family key (creative_stage_moves.family_key).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.campaign_id IS 'Meta scaling campaign id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.campaign_name IS 'Campaign name.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.adset_id IS 'Meta ad set id ('''' when unknown).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.adset_name IS 'Ad set name.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.ads IS 'Distinct Meta ads of the creative that spent in this ad set since the move.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.spend IS 'Spend since the move, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.purchases IS 'Purchases (Meta-reported here) since the move.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.revenue IS 'Purchase value since the move, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.first_day IS 'First day with spend there.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_placements.last_day IS 'Last day with spend there.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.creative_scaling_benchmarks IS 'Benchmarks of the Test to scale page: creatives, spend, purchases and revenue by basis, product and period. Grain: one row per (basis, product_slug, day_from, day_to). Source: public.scaling_benchmarks. Refresh: on demand. Coverage: the periods the Test to scale page compares against.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.creative_scaling_benchmarks.basis IS '''meta'' (Meta''s own reporting), ''upstack_nc'' (Upstack new customers) or ''upstack_all'' (Upstack all orders).';
