COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.product_slug IS 'Product the line belongs to.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.line_code IS 'L01.. / B01.. / BF01.. (unique per product).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.cluster IS 'Market cluster.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.icp IS 'Ideal customer profile / persona.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.pain_point IS 'Pain point.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.emotional_trigger IS 'Emotional trigger (can be NULL).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.story IS 'Short story the ad would tell (15 words or fewer).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.cluster_color IS 'Hex colour of the cluster in the sheet.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.sort_order IS 'Communication Overview order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_taxonomy_lines.added_after_tagging IS 'true = the line was added after the product''s ads were tagged.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.tag_line_ingredients IS 'The ingredients that address each taxonomy line: one row per line and ingredient with what it attacks and what it supports. Grain: one row per ingredient_id. Source: public.line_ingredients joined to taxonomy_lines and products. Refresh: when the taxonomy is reloaded. Coverage: every line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_line_ingredients.ingredient_id IS 'Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_line_ingredients.line_id IS 'taxonomy_lines.id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_line_ingredients.product_slug IS 'Product of the line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_line_ingredients.line_code IS 'taxonomy_lines.line_code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_line_ingredients.ingredient IS 'Nutrient / active compound that addresses the pain point (e.g. Zinc, Heme Iron, Glucosamine).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_line_ingredients.attacks IS '''What It Attacks'': the mechanism it counters.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_line_ingredients.supports IS '''What It Supports''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tag_line_ingredients.sort_order IS 'Order within the line.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.tracker_tags IS 'Every tag ever written to a tracker row (current and superseded), joined to the tracker row, product and taxonomy line. Filter is_current for what stands now. Grain: one row per tag_id. Source: public.ad_tags joined to tracker_rows, products and taxonomy_lines (the extra json is left out). Refresh: when tags load or the auto-tagger runs. Coverage: every live tracker row. Caveats: A tracker row has at most one CURRENT tag per tag_set; analytics.creative_tracker already shows the current tag of the product''s own tag set. | confidence / method say how sure the tagger was: low-confidence and copy-only tags are weaker evidence.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.tag_id IS 'Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.tracker_row_id IS 'tracker_rows.id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.concept_id IS 'Creative Tracker concept id of the tagged row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.family_key IS 'Tracker ad family key (join to creative_tracker / creative_family_metrics).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.product_slug IS 'Product of the tracker row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.tag_set IS '''linemap'' | ''tracker''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.version IS 'Tagging cycle, e.g. ''linemap-v2-2026-11-03'', ''tracker-live''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.is_current IS 'true for the tag in force.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.line_id IS 'taxonomy_lines.id (linemap tags).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.line_code IS 'taxonomy_lines.line_code the tag points at (NULL for tracker-set tags).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.cluster IS 'Market cluster.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.icp IS 'ICP / persona.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.pain_point IS 'Pain point.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.emotional_trigger IS 'Emotional trigger.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.confidence IS 'high | medium | low | NULL.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.method IS 'How it was tagged: ''image'', ''video: 4 frames + Whisper transcript'', ''text only'', ''no picture (copy only)'', ''video: thumbnail + no audio'' ...';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.seen IS '''What Was Seen'': the tagger''s description of the creative.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.why IS 'Why the line was chosen.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.runner_up IS 'Second-best line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.copy_only_line IS 'Line the copy-only first pass picked when different.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.tagger IS 'Who / what tagged it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_tags.tagged_at IS 'When the tag was written.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.tracker_hooks IS 'The hook of each tracker row: the first spoken line and the first on-screen text, joined to the tracker row and product. Grain: one row per tracker_row_id. Source: public.ad_hooks joined to tracker_rows and products. Refresh: when hooks are reloaded (etl.load_hooks). Coverage: the current tracker rows that had something readable (a silent video or an ad with no copy has no hook). Caveats: hook_source says where the hook came from (video transcript, image, copy). Rows with nothing readable have no hook.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.tracker_row_id IS 'tracker_rows.id (primary key).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.concept_id IS 'Creative Tracker concept id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.family_key IS 'Tracker ad family key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.product_slug IS 'Product of the tracker row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.hook IS 'The one-line hook.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.spoken IS 'First spoken line (video audio / transcript).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.on_screen IS 'On-image headline / first on-screen text.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.hook_source IS 'spoken | on_screen | both | copy | none.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.confidence IS 'high | medium | low.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.note IS 'Extractor remark.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.version IS 'Extraction cycle, e.g. ''hooks-v1-2026-11-05''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.extractor IS 'Who produced it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.tracker_hooks.extracted_at IS 'When the row was written.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.priorities_snapshots IS 'One row per weekly creative priorities snapshot: when it was built, the data it used and how many rows it holds. Grain: one row per week_start (the Sunday, Pacific). Source: public.creative_priorities_snapshots without the json blobs (they are flattened into the other priorities_* views). Refresh: Sundays in the nightly etl (etl.creative_priorities). Coverage: from the first week the page ran.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_snapshots.week_start IS 'The Sunday (Pacific) the snapshot belongs to (primary key).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_snapshots.built_at IS 'When the snapshot was last written.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_snapshots.data_through IS 'Last day of Meta data the snapshot used.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_snapshots.basis IS 'Numbers basis of the scoring: ''meta'' (Meta-reported).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_snapshots.row_count IS 'Number of rows in the snapshot (every line plus manual and proposal rows).';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.priorities_thresholds IS 'Every threshold and weight the week was scored with (HIT_SPEND, TOP_SPEND, JUDGED_SPEND, MIN_LINE_SPEND, the score weights ...), one row per (week, name). Grain: one row per (week_start, name). Source: public.creative_priorities_snapshots.thresholds, flattened. Refresh: Sundays. Coverage: every snapshot. Caveats: value is text: cast it. Scoring counts a hit at HIT_SPEND = $1,000; the displayed hit rate uses TOP_SPEND = $10,000 (etl/creative_priorities.py).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_thresholds.week_start IS 'The Sunday (Pacific) the snapshot belongs to (primary key).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_thresholds.name IS 'Constant name as in etl/creative_priorities.py.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_thresholds.value IS 'Its value for that week, as text.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.priorities_baselines IS 'The product averages each line is compared with (ROAS, CPA, hit rate, spend, funnel counts), one numeric row per (week, product, metric). Grain: one row per (week_start, product_slug, metric). Source: public.creative_priorities_snapshots.baselines, numeric entries only. Refresh: Sundays. Coverage: every snapshot. Caveats: Metrics include roas, cpa, hit_rate (scoring basis, $1,000 over mature tested ads) and the funnel counts; see priorities_concepts for the per-line figures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_baselines.week_start IS 'The snapshot''s Sunday.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_baselines.product_slug IS 'Product the baseline is for.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_baselines.metric IS 'Baseline metric name as in the snapshot.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_baselines.value IS 'Its numeric value.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.priorities_concepts IS 'Every row of every weekly priorities snapshot, flattened: the line (cluster, ICP, pain point), its action section and status, score, confidence and the numbers behind it (Meta-reported, with Upstack new-customer ROAS beside them). Grain: one row per (week_start, row of the snapshot). Source: public.creative_priorities_snapshots.rows, flattened with the numeric fields typed. Refresh: Sundays. Coverage: every snapshot. Caveats: Two hit rates exist. hit_rate / hit_rate_index = SCORING: share of mature (>= 14 days old) tested ads that reached $1,000, shrunk toward the product average; the CSV export''s hit_rate columns are this one. DISPLAY (what Josh calls a hit): ads_10k_plus_spend / ads_launched, ads that reached $10,000 since launch out of every launched ad. Name which one you mean. | Numbers are Meta-reported (roas = purchase value / spend); nc_roas is Upstack new-customer ROAS. ROAS is NULL under $100 spend. section / status use the current vocabulary (older snapshots are stored in the old words).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.week_start IS 'The snapshot''s Sunday.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.product_slug IS 'vita-bull | beef-liver | boneflex (rows of manual concepts keep their typed product).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.section IS 'Action section the row sits in (make more, revive, test, stop, hold, add to sheet, proposed, competitor, everything else).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.status IS 'Line status (WORKING, RISING, FADED, COLLAPSED, TOO EARLY, UNTESTED, NOT WORKING, AVERAGE ...).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.rank IS 'Rank inside its product and section.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.line_code IS 'taxonomy_lines.line_code (NULL for manual and proposed rows).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.cluster IS 'Market cluster.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.icp IS 'ICP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.pain_point IS 'Pain point.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.emotional_trigger IS 'Emotional trigger of the line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.story IS 'Story of the line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.concepts IS 'New concepts to brief for the row this week.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.score IS '0-100 iterate score (35% economics, 20% hit rate, 20% room, 15% momentum, 10% size).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.confidence IS 'high | medium | low.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.flags IS 'Risk flags, joined with ''; '' (thin sample, weak tags, few ads, Upstack new-customer ROAS below product average).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.why IS 'One-paragraph reason the row was chosen.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.is_manual IS 'true for a concept typed by hand on the page.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.spend IS 'Since-launch spend of the line, Meta, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.purchases IS 'Since-launch Meta-reported purchases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.roas IS 'Since-launch Meta ROAS (NULL under $100 spend).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.cpa IS 'Since-launch cost per purchase.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.roas_index IS 'Shrunk since-launch ROAS / the product''s ROAS.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.ads IS 'Ads of the line that spent.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.judged IS 'Ads that spent $100 or more.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.hits IS 'Mature judged ads that reached $1,000 (scoring hits).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.mature IS 'Judged ads at least 14 days old (the scoring hit-rate denominator).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.hit_rate IS 'SCORING hit rate: hits / mature (the $1,000 threshold).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.hit_rate_index IS 'Shrunk hit rate / the product''s.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.spend_30d IS 'Spend in the 30 days ending at data_through.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.roas_30d IS 'ROAS over those 30 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.spend_14d IS 'Spend in the 14 days ending at data_through.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.roas_14d IS 'ROAS over those 14 days (NULL under $100).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.nc_roas IS 'Upstack new-customer ROAS since launch.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.nc_cpa IS 'Upstack new-customer CPA since launch.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.nc_purchases IS 'Upstack new customers credited since launch.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.live_ads IS 'Ads of the line that spent in the last days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.ads_launched IS 'DISPLAY funnel: ads of the line launched (tracker rows with a launch date or any spend).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.ads_under_100_spend IS 'Launched ads under $100 spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.ads_100_plus_spend IS 'Launched ads at $100 or more.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_concepts.ads_10k_plus_spend IS 'Launched ads at $10,000 or more (the display hits).';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.priorities_manual_concepts IS 'Concepts typed in by hand on the priorities page (not scored): product, section, line, why now and status. Grain: one row per manual_id. Source: public.creative_priorities_manual. Refresh: on demand (edited by a person). Coverage: every manual concept.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.manual_id IS 'Primary key (bigserial).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.product IS '''vita-bull'' | ''beef-liver'' | ''boneflex''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.section IS 'Page section the concept sits in: ''iterate'' | ''faded'' | ''new'' | ''other''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.cluster IS 'Market cluster (catalog value or typed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.icp IS 'ICP (catalog value or typed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.pain_point IS 'Pain point (catalog value or typed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.story IS 'Story; empty when none.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.notes IS 'Free-text notes, up to 2,000 characters, line breaks kept.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.why_now IS 'Optional short why-now / what-to-test line, up to 300 characters.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.status IS '''open'' (shown) or ''done'' (hidden until Show done is ticked).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.new_cluster IS 'True when the cluster is not in the catalog for that product.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.new_icp IS 'True when the ICP is not in the catalog under that cluster.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.new_pain_point IS 'True when the pain point is not in the catalog under that ICP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.new_story IS 'True when the story is typed text not in the catalog for that pain point.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.created_at IS 'When the concept was added.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.updated_at IS 'When it was last edited or its status changed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.priorities_manual_concepts.done_at IS 'When it was marked done; NULL while open.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.production_assignments IS 'One concept given to one vendor to make for one week: the line, the brief and creative links, the timestamp of each step and the tracker concepts it became. Grain: one row per assignment_id. Source: public.creative_priorities_assignments without created_by / updated_by (who made a change is not exposed). Refresh: on demand (the production board and the nightly etl.assignment_tags). Coverage: from the day production tracking started. Caveats: stage_from_assignment reads only the assignment''s own fields; the app also takes the furthest stage its linked tracker rows show (join tracker_concept_ids to creative_tracker.concept_id and read status). | vendor_note is the note the vendor sees; note is internal.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.assignment_id IS 'Primary key (bigserial).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.concept_key IS 'Stable concept handle: ''line:<taxonomy_lines.id>'' when the row has a line, ''manual:<id>'' for a manual concept, else ''text:<product>|<cluster>|<icp>|<pain point>'' (lowercased, spaces collapsed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.product IS '''vita-bull'' | ''beef-liver'' | ''boneflex''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.vendor IS 'Vendor, spelled as in the Creative Tracker Vendor column (Madre, Victoria, TrybeDCShop, TrybeOrion, 10xROAS, Internal, PuredMedia, CreateMastery, OpenProgram).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.line_id IS 'taxonomy_lines.id at assign time; NULL for manual or proposed concepts. No foreign key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.manual_id IS 'creative_priorities_manual.id for a manual concept; NULL otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.line_code IS 'Line code (for example BL12) at assign time; empty when none.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.cluster IS 'Market cluster at assign time.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.icp IS 'ICP at assign time.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.pain_point IS 'Pain point at assign time.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.story IS 'Story at assign time; empty when none.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.section_at_assign IS 'Action the concept had when assigned: ''revive'' | ''make_more'' | ''test'' | ''add'' | ''stop'' | ''hold'' (rows written before 2026-11-10 hold the old section names ''faded'' | ''iterate'' | ''new'' | ''proposal'' | ''competitor'' | ''rest'' | ''other'', shown as the new Action).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.format_code IS 'Creative format chosen when assigning or later (creative_formats.code, foreign key); NULL when none was chosen. Set by a signed-in user only; a vendor sees it but cannot change it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.note IS 'Note typed when assigning or changing the assignment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.vendor_note IS 'Note typed by the vendor on their own link page.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.for_week IS 'The Monday of the week the vendor works on it (a CHECK enforces a Monday).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.brief_url IS 'Link to the brief; NULL until added.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.creative_url IS 'Link to the finished creative; NULL until added.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.brief_at IS 'When the brief link was first added; NULL until then.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.creative_at IS 'When the creative link was first added; NULL until then.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.ready_at IS 'When someone clicked Ready to launch; NULL if not (or cleared).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.launched_at IS 'When it was marked launched by hand; NULL if not. A linked tracker row with status 8 or 9 also counts as launched.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.dropped_at IS 'When the assignment was dropped (soft cancel); NULL while active. Rows are never deleted.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.tracker_concept_ids IS 'Creative Tracker Concept IDs of the ads made from this assignment, entered by hand.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.stage_from_assignment IS 'dropped | launched | ready | creative_in | brief_sent | assigned, from dropped_at, launched_at, ready_at, creative_url and brief_url in that order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.created_at IS 'When the assignment was created.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_assignments.updated_at IS 'When it was last changed.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.production_formats IS 'The creative formats (static, short video, ...) an assignment can carry. Grain: one row per format_code. Source: public.creative_formats. Refresh: on change. Coverage: a handful of rows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_formats.format_code IS 'Short code (primary key), F1 to F6.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_formats.name IS 'What the format is, shown in the pick list.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_formats.length IS 'Typical running time, as text (for example ''45 to 90s''); NULL when not set.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_formats.sort IS 'Order in the pick list (ascending).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.production_formats.active IS 'True while the format can be chosen on a new assignment.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.competitor_brands IS 'The competitor brands tracked in the Meta Ad Library and when each was last read. Grain: one row per brand. Source: public.competitor_brands without last_error. Refresh: Sundays (etl.competitor_ads). Coverage: every tracked brand.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_brands.brand IS 'Brand name (primary key), as shown in the views.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_brands.product_type IS 'Free text: what the brand sells (beef organ capsules, joint supplement ...).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_brands.search_phrases IS 'Exact phrases searched in the Ad Library (brand name, landing domain); results are filtered by name_match.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_brands.name_match IS 'Case-insensitive regex the advertiser (page) name must match; creator ads named ''X with Brand'' are dropped.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_brands.active IS 'False retires the brand without deleting its history.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_brands.last_attempt_at IS 'Last time a run tried this brand.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_brands.last_ok_at IS 'Last time the brand loaded without error.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_brands.last_ad_count IS 'Active US ads read in the last good run (a top slice by impressions: capped at about 150 cards per phrase).';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.competitor_ads IS 'Weekly snapshot of each competitor ad found in the Meta Ad Library: format, copy, hook, landing page and how long it has been running. Grain: one row per (week_start, library_id). Source: public.competitor_ads. Refresh: Sundays (etl.competitor_ads). Coverage: from the first week the tracker ran. Caveats: Running a long time is not proven performance: the Ad Library shows no spend or results.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.week_start IS 'Monday (Pacific) of the week of the run.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.library_id IS 'Meta Ad Library ID.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.brand IS 'competitor_brands.brand.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.advertiser IS 'Page name shown on the card.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.start_date IS '''Started running on'' date (resets on re-upload).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.days_running IS 'seen_on minus start_date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.variant_count IS 'Ads sharing this creative and text (card says ''N ads use this creative and text''), else 1.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.format IS '''video'' or ''image''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.primary_text IS 'Ad copy as shown (up to 2,500 characters).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.headline IS 'Card headline (first line after the landing domain that is not a button label).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.hook IS 'First sentence of the copy, else the headline.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.landing_url IS 'Landing domain and path (tracking query removed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.concept_key IS 'Brand + hash of the first 160 characters of normalised copy: groups near-duplicate copy into one concept.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.seen_on IS 'Date the Library was read (Pacific); for carried rows the original date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_ads.carried_from IS 'NULL for fresh rows; for carried-forward rows the week_start they were copied from.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.competitor_concepts IS 'Competitor ads grouped into concepts per week and mapped to our product, line, cluster, ICP and pain point (or flagged as a new angle). Grain: one row per (week_start, brand, concept_key). Source: public.competitor_concepts (a view over competitor_ads and competitor_concept_class). Refresh: Sundays. Coverage: every week with a snapshot. Caveats: The mapping to our lines is a model''s classification (confidence says how sure); new-angle rows are concepts that fit no existing line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.week_start IS 'Monday (Pacific) of the run week.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.brand IS 'Brand.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.concept_key IS 'Concept (near-duplicate copy of one brand).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.first_ad_start_date IS 'Earliest start date among the concept''s ads.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.days_running IS 'Max days running among the concept''s ads (as of as_of).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.variant_count IS 'Ads sharing the creative / copy, summed over the concept''s cards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.format IS '''video'' or ''image'' of the longest-running ad.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.hook IS 'First sentence of the longest-running ad''s copy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.primary_text_excerpt IS 'First 280 characters of that ad''s copy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.mapped_product IS '''vita-bull'' | ''beef-liver'' | ''boneflex'' | ''none'' | NULL.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.line_code IS 'Lonvera catalog line, NULL for NEW / out-of-category / unclassified.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.cluster IS 'Market cluster.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.icp IS 'ICP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.pain_point IS 'Pain point.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.confidence IS 'high | medium | low (unclassified = low).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.is_new_angle IS 'No catalog line covers it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.new_angle_label IS 'Label of the NEW angle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.as_of IS 'Date the Library was read.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.competitor_concepts.is_stale IS 'Carried forward or older than 8 days.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.catalog IS 'One row per analytics view: its domain, what it is, its grain, the first and last day it covers where it has days, and a row-count estimate. Start here to find which view answers a question. Grain: one row per analytics view (this view itself is listed too). Source: generated from docs/schema/descriptions.py into migration 230 (descriptions, domains) and the first / last day of each view''s base table; row_estimate = pg_class.reltuples. Refresh: first_day / last_day read the base tables live; the descriptions change only with a migration. Coverage: every analytics view. Caveats: row_estimate is Postgres''s planner estimate of the base table (NULL until the table is first analysed), not a count; run count(*) when you need the exact number. | first_day / last_day are NULL for views without a day axis (dimensions, definitions, scenarios). Read data_coverage for per-source freshness of the marketing data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.catalog.view_name IS 'Name of the view in the analytics schema.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.catalog.domain IS 'marketing | attribution | orders | creative | tags | priorities | production | projection | inventory | cohorts | pacing | competitors | pipeline.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.catalog.description IS 'What the view is (its purpose text).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.catalog.grain IS 'What one row is.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.catalog.first_day IS 'First day the view''s base table holds (NULL when not a time series).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.catalog.last_day IS 'Last day the base table holds.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.catalog.row_estimate IS 'Planner row-count estimate of the base table.';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.metric_glossary IS 'The canonical definition of every headline metric (ROAS, CPA, NC ROAS, CPM, frequency, hit rate, payback, ...): formula, the view and columns that hold the inputs, the default basis, the other bases and the traps. The same rows as the ''metrics'' key of docs/schema.json. Grain: one row per metric name. Source: generated from the METRICS list in docs/schema/descriptions.py into migration 230; every formula was taken from the code (the file is named in source or traps). Refresh: changes only with a migration. Coverage: every metric of the glossary (see the Metrics section of docs/DATA_SCHEMA.md). Caveats: other_bases and traps are text arrays: unnest them or read them whole. Read the default basis before quoting a number and name the basis in the answer.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.metric_glossary.name IS 'Machine name, e.g. nc_roas.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.metric_glossary.label IS 'Display name.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.metric_glossary.formula IS 'The formula in plain words and column names.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.metric_glossary.source IS 'analytics.<view>.<column(s)> that hold the inputs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.metric_glossary.default_basis IS 'The basis to use unless asked otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.metric_glossary.other_bases IS 'The other bases that exist for the metric.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.metric_glossary.traps IS 'Ways the metric is read wrongly, with the code file the rule comes from.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.metric_glossary.domain IS 'Domain of the metric (same list as analytics.catalog).';
